// Adversarial stress: Burnout protocol under sustained chaos input — Dense layout.
//
// Burnout's 4-system pipeline: burnout_update_heat (fills heat while moving,
// drains while stationary, clamps to [0.0, 1.0], arms mega_bump_charged at full,
// fires still-threshold instant-drain + BurnoutSpeedBoost + shockwave),
// burnout_on_bump (consumes BumpPerformed, installs BurnoutDamageBoost on bolt,
// resets heat, dispatches shockwave), burnout_amplify_damage (consumes
// BoltImpactCell on boosted bolts, emits DamageDealt<Cell> with
// BURNOUT_SENTINEL source_chip), and burnout_cleanup_node (OnExit, removes all
// Burnout components). This stress scenario targets five failure paths:
//
//   1. Heat clamp boundary — moving/stationary race on the same frame:
//      burnout_update_heat runs after BreakerSystems::Move. Chaos input
//      produces frames where the breaker transitions from moving to stationary
//      (or vice versa) and the speed-squared threshold (> EPSILON) is crossed
//      exactly at the frame boundary. If the fill / drain arithmetic overshoots
//      (e.g., dt / fill_duration > 1.0 - current heat when heat is near 1.0),
//      heat can transiently exceed 1.0 before the `.min(1.0)` clamp in the
//      moving branch. BurnoutHeatClamped fires if heat drifts outside [0.0,
//      1.0]. Dense layout with action_prob 0.7 keeps the breaker oscillating
//      rapidly between moving and still, maximising transition density.
//
//   2. still_timer sign — still-threshold fire + reset interaction:
//      When still_timer crosses still_threshold (1.5 s), the system sets
//      heat = 0.0 and still_timer = 0.0. If a subsequent tick adds dt again
//      before the reset propagates (e.g., a double-execution bug or wrong
//      ordering), still_timer can go negative. BurnoutHeatClamped checks
//      still_timer >= 0.0 every frame.
//
//   3. mega_bump_charged double-consume path: burnout_on_bump runs after
//      BreakerSystems::GradeBump and after burnout_update_heat. If the
//      BumpPerformed reader is not drained when Burnout is inactive (before
//      InjectProtocol fires at frame 10), retroactive message processing on
//      frame 11 can fire burnout_on_bump against an entity that already had
//      its charge set by burnout_update_heat in the same frame — resulting in
//      a BurnoutDamageBoost on a bolt that has already bounced. The
//      still_timer then gets doubly reset. NoNaN catches any NaN cascade; the
//      in-body reader.clear() guard is the protection under test here.
//
//   4. Shockwave entity accumulation under rapid mega-bumps: each
//      mega_bump_charged consume fires a shockwave via commands.fire_effect.
//      Dense layout with action_prob 0.7 means the breaker reaches heat = 1.0
//      repeatedly across 3000 frames and each still-threshold fire also
//      dispatches a shockwave. NoEntityLeaks guards shockwave entity cleanup;
//      NoNaN catches position NaN from a shockwave expanding beyond the
//      playfield without bound checks.
//
//   5. burnout_cleanup_node cross-node isolation: allow_early_end: false
//      triggers repeated node restarts. On each OnExit(NodeState::Playing),
//      burnout_cleanup_node removes BurnoutHeat, BurnoutSpeedBoost, and
//      BurnoutDamageBoost. If the node exit races with a BumpPerformed message
//      buffered from the final tick of the dying node, burnout_on_bump (which
//      runs every FixedUpdate, gated in-body) may install BurnoutDamageBoost on
//      a bolt entity that is already mid-despawn. The next node's
//      burnout_update_heat then lazy-inserts BurnoutHeat::default() — if the
//      cleanup did not fully clear the prior breaker, the new node begins with
//      heat > 0.0 and still_timer > 0.0. BurnoutHeatClamped catches any heat
//      outside [0.0, 1.0]; NoEntityLeaks catches the orphaned DamageBoost
//      component on a stale bolt entity.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false sustains pressure across node
// restarts. 16 runs explore diverse Dense cell arrangements and heat-fill
// timing distributions.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
        BurnoutHeatClamped,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 6631,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "Burnout")),
    ],
)
